{
  "requirement": "`ValidationCache::new()` creates an empty cache for running criteria without\nan agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> ValidationCache<D> {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.new` has two obligations: `ValidationCache::new()` returns an empty cache, and that cache has no agent.\n\n- **No agent:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `ValidationCache::<TestDomain>::new()` and asserts `cache.agent.is_none()`. This covers the \"without an agent\" obligation.\n- **Empty cache:** The same test asserts `cache.sources.is_none()` and that the `outlines` map is empty. The `ValidationCache` struct in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` also has `nodes`, `source_addresses` and `usage`. This test cannot read the private `nodes` field, and it does not check `source_addresses` or `usage`. `ValidationCache::new` in `domain.rs` is just `Self::default()`. It has no conditionals and no logic of its own, so a `new` that pre-populated those fields is not a plausible failure. The remaining fields therefore need no separate assertion.\n- **Integration use:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` is also marked as a test of `new`. It starts from a fresh cache, and its first `from_path` call fails because nothing is cached or on disk yet. It then shows the cache filling on demand, which supports the \"empty\" obligation.\n\nI found no gap.",
